  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The gathering has an announcement board and several return points, but the team does not track guests individually.\", \"decision\": \"How should the team handle cups that have not returned on time?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers visit the return points with a reminder sign and then update the announcement board with the remaining overdue count. The reminder reaches likely return locations before the count is refreshed.\nThe team posts the number of overdue cups on the announcement board and directs guests to the return points. A shared reminder can prompt returns without identifying borrowers.\nThe team announces a short return period on the board and gathers updates from return points after it ends. Guests have a clear shared moment to bring cups back."
    }
  ],
